  "story": {
    "language": "en",
    "translationLanguage": "zh-Hant",
    "textEn": "Look at three words: in, on, and at. Use in with years, months, and seasons. We say in winter and in autumn. We also say in 2024 and in April. For parts of the day, say in the morning, in the afternoon, and in the evening. Now, on. Use on with days and dates. Say on Monday and on December 25. We also say on my birthday. For a morning on one day, say on Monday morning. Next, at. Use at with a time on the clock. Say at five in the afternoon and at seven in the morning. We also say at noon, at midnight, and at night. These words help us talk about time. Some time words do not need in, on, or at. Say this morning and next Monday. Also say last year and every day. Do not put in, on, or at before these four time phrases.",
    "textZh": "看看這三個字：in、on 和 at。年、月和季節使用 in。我們說 in winter（在冬天）和 in autumn（在秋天）。我們也說 in 2024（在二〇二四年）和 in April（在四月）。一天中的時段可以說 in the morning（在早上）、in the afternoon（在下午）和 in the evening（在傍晚或晚上）。接著是 on。星期和日期使用 on。說 on Monday（在星期一）和 on December 25（在十二月二十五日）。我們也說 on my birthday（在我的生日當天）。指定某一天的早上時，可以說 on Monday morning（在星期一早上）。接著是 at。時鐘上的時間點使用 at。說 at five in the afternoon（在下午五點）和 at seven in the morning（在早上七點），對應圖上的 at 5:00 p.m. 和 at 7:00 a.m.。我們也說 at noon（在中午）、at midnight（在午夜）和 at night（在夜晚）。這些字幫助我們表達時間。有些時間表達不用加 in、on 或 at。說 this morning（今天早上）和 next Monday（下星期一）。也可以說 last year（去年）和 every day（每天）。這四種時間片語前面不加 in、on 或 at。",
